[{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative makes it easier for software developers to master in-demand skills. Through hands-on courses designed to minimize setup and maximize learning, Educative helps developers and engineering teams become more productive and successful.\nToday, millions of developers and engineering teams love learning with Educative. We're also expanding beyond software development with Fenzo, our newly launched AI-powered learning platform built to help a broader range of learners understand what they're studying, not just get quick answers.\nEducative is a fast-growing and even faster-moving software startup (recently ranked in the Deloitte Technology Fast 500 as one of the world's fastest growing tech companies). Your work as a Community Manager will be vital to the objectives of the company and Marketing team, especially as we grow Fenzo's community from the ground up. Your output will be customer-facing, so your impact will be visible and meaningful.\nEducative's growing community of developers, engineering leaders, and now Fenzo learners will depend on you!\n","additional":"<div>\n<p><strong>About Educative:</strong></p>\n<p>Educative makes it easier for software developers to master in-demand skills. Through hands-on courses designed to minimize setup and maximize learning, Educative helps developers and engineering teams become more productive and successful.</p>\n<p>Today, millions of developers and engineering teams love learning with Educative. We're also expanding beyond software development with Fenzo, our newly launched AI-powered learning platform built to help a broader range of learners understand what they're studying, not just get quick answers.</p>\n<p>Educative is a fast-growing and even faster-moving software startup (recently ranked in the Deloitte Technology Fast 500 as one of the world's fastest growing tech companies). Your work as a Community Manager will be vital to the objectives of the company and Marketing team, especially as we grow Fenzo's community from the ground up. Your output will be customer-facing, so your impact will be visible and meaningful.</p>\n<p>Educative's growing community of developers, engineering leaders, and now Fenzo learners will depend on you!</p>\n</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Marketing and Sales","location":"Lahore","team":"Marketing","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1784795318847,"descriptionPlain":"Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.\nEducative is looking for an enthusiastic Community Manager to build and grow our presence across the communities Fenzo serves — students, educators, professionals, and self-learners alike. This is an early-career role ideal for someone who lives and breathes online spaces, is comfortable writing content that resonates, and is excited to wear a lot of hats across community, content, and outreach.\nAs part of Educative's marketing team, you'll be the person who finds where Fenzo's current and future users already gather, shows up there authentically, creates content that speaks to them, and builds real relationships on Fenzo's behalf. This role isn't narrowly scoped — you should be just as comfortable writing a LinkedIn post as you are moderating a Discord server or reaching out to a potential partner or advocate.\nWhat You'll Do\nCommunity Discovery & Presence\nIdentify and map where Fenzo's audiences spend time online — this includes student-focused spaces like subreddits, Discord servers, and campus forums, but also educator communities, professional groups, and self-learner spaces on X, LinkedIn, and elsewhere.\nBuild genuine presence in these spaces before pushing any Fenzo message — understanding the culture and norms of each community first.\nContinuously scout new platforms and communities as audience behavior shifts, so Fenzo is never late to where the conversation is happening.\nCommunity Building & Engagement\nActively participate in relevant communities, answering questions, sharing useful resources, and sparking genuine dialogue — not just posting promotional content.\nBuild relationships with community moderators, active members, and potential advocates (student, educator, or professional) who can become organic voices for Fenzo.\nCreate and nurture Fenzo's own community spaces (Discord, subreddit, or similar) as a home base for engaged users.\nContent Creation\nWrite and publish content for channels like LinkedIn, X, and Reddit, tailored to how each platform's audience actually consumes content.\nHelp shape Fenzo's voice across written social content — posts, threads, comments, and community responses.\nCollaborate with Marketing and Product to turn Fenzo's product updates and capabilities into content that resonates with real users.\nOutreach & Relationship Building\nConduct outreach to students, teachers, and other potential users or advocates to introduce Fenzo and build genuine relationships.\nIdentify and connect with potential creators, educators, or community voices who could authentically speak to Fenzo's value.\nHelp manage outreach relationships end-to-end — first contact, follow-up, and ongoing engagement.\nInsight Gathering\nListen closely to what users across different communities are struggling with, what language they use to describe their pain points, and what alternatives they're discussing.\nReport community feedback, sentiment, and trends back to Marketing and Product teams to shape strategy and messaging.\n \nQualifications\n\nMust-Haves\nGenuine familiarity with online communities relevant to Fenzo's audience — particularly student spaces, but also comfort navigating educator, professional, or self-learner communities.\nActive, genuine presence on platforms like Reddit, Discord, X, or LinkedIn, ideally with a track record of engagement.\nStrong written communication skills — comfortable writing content and initiating outreach in a way that feels authentic rather than corporate.\nComfortable wearing many hats — someone who can go from writing a LinkedIn post, to moderating a Discord, to reaching out to a potential partner, all in the same day.\nNice-to-Haves\nExperience moderating or running a Discord server, subreddit, or similar community.\nPrior experience running or growing a personal or brand social/content presence.\nFamiliarity with the ed-tech, education, or professional learning space.\nPrevious involvement in student organizations, educator networks, or professional communities.\nComfortable with cold outreach and building relationships from scratch.\n","description":"<p>Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.</p>\n<p>Educative is looking for an enthusiastic Community Manager to build and grow our presence across the communities Fenzo serves — students, educators, professionals, and self-learners alike. This is an early-career role ideal for someone who lives and breathes online spaces, is comfortable writing content that resonates, and is excited to wear a lot of hats across community, content, and outreach.</p>\n<p>As part of Educative's marketing team, you'll be the person who finds where Fenzo's current and future users already gather, shows up there authentically, creates content that speaks to them, and builds real relationships on Fenzo's behalf. This role isn't narrowly scoped — you should be just as comfortable writing a LinkedIn post as you are moderating a Discord server or reaching out to a potential partner or advocate.</p>\n<p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Community Discovery &amp; Presence</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Identify and map where Fenzo's audiences spend time online — this includes student-focused spaces like subreddits, Discord servers, and campus forums, but also educator communities, professional groups, and self-learner spaces on X, LinkedIn, and elsewhere.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Build genuine presence in these spaces before pushing any Fenzo message — understanding the culture and norms of each community first.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Continuously scout new platforms and communities as audience behavior shifts, so Fenzo is never late to where the conversation is happening.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Community Building &amp; Engagement</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Actively participate in relevant communities, answering questions, sharing useful resources, and sparking genuine dialogue — not just posting promotional content.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Build relationships with community moderators, active members, and potential advocates (student, educator, or professional) who can become organic voices for Fenzo.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Create and nurture Fenzo's own community spaces (Discord, subreddit, or similar) as a home base for engaged users.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Content Creation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Write and publish content for channels like LinkedIn, X, and Reddit, tailored to how each platform's audience actually consumes content.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Help shape Fenzo's voice across written social content — posts, threads, comments, and community responses.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Collaborate with Marketing and Product to turn Fenzo's product updates and capabilities into content that resonates with real users.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Outreach &amp; Relationship Building</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Conduct outreach to students, teachers, and other potential users or advocates to introduce Fenzo and build genuine relationships.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Identify and connect with potential creators, educators, or community voices who could authentically speak to Fenzo's value.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Help manage outreach relationships end-to-end — first contact, follow-up, and ongoing engagement.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Insight Gathering</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Listen closely to what users across different communities are struggling with, what language they use to describe their pain points, and what alternatives they're discussing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Report community feedback, sentiment, and trends back to Marketing and Product teams to shape strategy and messaging.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Must-Haves</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Genuine familiarity with online communities relevant to Fenzo's audience — particularly student spaces, but also comfort navigating educator, professional, or self-learner communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Active, genuine presence on platforms like Reddit, Discord, X, or LinkedIn, ideally with a track record of engagement.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Strong written communication skills — comfortable writing content and initiating outreach in a way that feels authentic rather than corporate.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Comfortable wearing many hats — someone who can go from writing a LinkedIn post, to moderating a Discord, to reaching out to a potential partner, all in the same day.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Nice-to-Haves</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Experience moderating or running a Discord server, subreddit, or similar community.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Prior experience running or growing a personal or brand social/content presence.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Familiarity with the ed-tech, education, or professional learning space.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Previous involvement in student organizations, educator networks, or professional communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Comfortable with cold outreach and building relationships from scratch.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>","id":"788f4c1f-5ee0-44ad-a3bd-2bdf98b6ea81","lists":[],"text":"Community Manager","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<p>Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most &mdash; through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes &mdash; and how it shows up in the world.</p>\n<p>Educative is looking for an enthusiastic Community Manager to build and grow our presence across the communities Fenzo serves &mdash; students, educators, professionals, and self-learners alike. This is an early-career role ideal for someone who lives and breathes online spaces, is comfortable writing content that resonates, and is excited to wear a lot of hats across community, content, and outreach.</p>\n<p>As part of Educative's marketing team, you'll be the person who finds where Fenzo's current and future users already gather, shows up there authentically, creates content that speaks to them, and builds real relationships on Fenzo's behalf. This role isn't narrowly scoped &mdash; you should be just as comfortable writing a LinkedIn post as you are moderating a Discord server or reaching out to a potential partner or advocate.</p>\n<p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Community Discovery &amp; Presence</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Identify and map where Fenzo's audiences spend time online &mdash; this includes student-focused spaces like subreddits, Discord servers, and campus forums, but also educator communities, professional groups, and self-learner spaces on X, LinkedIn, and elsewhere.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Build genuine presence in these spaces before pushing any Fenzo message &mdash; understanding the culture and norms of each community first.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Continuously scout new platforms and communities as audience behavior shifts, so Fenzo is never late to where the conversation is happening.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Community Building &amp; Engagement</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Actively participate in relevant communities, answering questions, sharing useful resources, and sparking genuine dialogue &mdash; not just posting promotional content.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Build relationships with community moderators, active members, and potential advocates (student, educator, or professional) who can become organic voices for Fenzo.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Create and nurture Fenzo's own community spaces (Discord, subreddit, or similar) as a home base for engaged users.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Content Creation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Write and publish content for channels like LinkedIn, X, and Reddit, tailored to how each platform's audience actually consumes content.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Help shape Fenzo's voice across written social content &mdash; posts, threads, comments, and community responses.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Collaborate with Marketing and Product to turn Fenzo's product updates and capabilities into content that resonates with real users.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Outreach &amp; Relationship Building</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Conduct outreach to students, teachers, and other potential users or advocates to introduce Fenzo and build genuine relationships.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Identify and connect with potential creators, educators, or community voices who could authentically speak to Fenzo's value.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Help manage outreach relationships end-to-end &mdash; first contact, follow-up, and ongoing engagement.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Insight Gathering</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Listen closely to what users across different communities are struggling with, what language they use to describe their pain points, and what alternatives they're discussing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Report community feedback, sentiment, and trends back to Marketing and Product teams to shape strategy and messaging.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Must-Haves</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Genuine familiarity with online communities relevant to Fenzo's audience &mdash; particularly student spaces, but also comfort navigating educator, professional, or self-learner communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Active, genuine presence on platforms like Reddit, Discord, X, or LinkedIn, ideally with a track record of engagement.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Strong written communication skills &mdash; comfortable writing content and initiating outreach in a way that feels authentic rather than corporate.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Comfortable wearing many hats &mdash; someone who can go from writing a LinkedIn post, to moderating a Discord, to reaching out to a potential partner, all in the same day.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Nice-to-Haves</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Experience moderating or running a Discord server, subreddit, or similar community.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Prior experience running or growing a personal or brand social/content presence.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Familiarity with the ed-tech, education, or professional learning space.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Previous involvement in student organizations, educator networks, or professional communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Comfortable with cold outreach and building relationships from scratch.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.\nEducative is looking for an enthusiastic Community Manager to build and grow our presence across the communities Fenzo serves — students, educators, professionals, and self-learners alike. This is an early-career role ideal for someone who lives and breathes online spaces, is comfortable writing content that resonates, and is excited to wear a lot of hats across community, content, and outreach.\nAs part of Educative's marketing team, you'll be the person who finds where Fenzo's current and future users already gather, shows up there authentically, creates content that speaks to them, and builds real relationships on Fenzo's behalf. This role isn't narrowly scoped — you should be just as comfortable writing a LinkedIn post as you are moderating a Discord server or reaching out to a potential partner or advocate.\nWhat You'll Do\nCommunity Discovery & Presence\nIdentify and map where Fenzo's audiences spend time online — this includes student-focused spaces like subreddits, Discord servers, and campus forums, but also educator communities, professional groups, and self-learner spaces on X, LinkedIn, and elsewhere.\nBuild genuine presence in these spaces before pushing any Fenzo message — understanding the culture and norms of each community first.\nContinuously scout new platforms and communities as audience behavior shifts, so Fenzo is never late to where the conversation is happening.\nCommunity Building & Engagement\nActively participate in relevant communities, answering questions, sharing useful resources, and sparking genuine dialogue — not just posting promotional content.\nBuild relationships with community moderators, active members, and potential advocates (student, educator, or professional) who can become organic voices for Fenzo.\nCreate and nurture Fenzo's own community spaces (Discord, subreddit, or similar) as a home base for engaged users.\nContent Creation\nWrite and publish content for channels like LinkedIn, X, and Reddit, tailored to how each platform's audience actually consumes content.\nHelp shape Fenzo's voice across written social content — posts, threads, comments, and community responses.\nCollaborate with Marketing and Product to turn Fenzo's product updates and capabilities into content that resonates with real users.\nOutreach & Relationship Building\nConduct outreach to students, teachers, and other potential users or advocates to introduce Fenzo and build genuine relationships.\nIdentify and connect with potential creators, educators, or community voices who could authentically speak to Fenzo's value.\nHelp manage outreach relationships end-to-end — first contact, follow-up, and ongoing engagement.\nInsight Gathering\nListen closely to what users across different communities are struggling with, what language they use to describe their pain points, and what alternatives they're discussing.\nReport community feedback, sentiment, and trends back to Marketing and Product teams to shape strategy and messaging.\n \nQualifications\n\nMust-Haves\nGenuine familiarity with online communities relevant to Fenzo's audience — particularly student spaces, but also comfort navigating educator, professional, or self-learner communities.\nActive, genuine presence on platforms like Reddit, Discord, X, or LinkedIn, ideally with a track record of engagement.\nStrong written communication skills — comfortable writing content and initiating outreach in a way that feels authentic rather than corporate.\nComfortable wearing many hats — someone who can go from writing a LinkedIn post, to moderating a Discord, to reaching out to a potential partner, all in the same day.\nNice-to-Haves\nExperience moderating or running a Discord server, subreddit, or similar community.\nPrior experience running or growing a personal or brand social/content presence.\nFamiliarity with the ed-tech, education, or professional learning space.\nPrevious involvement in student organizations, educator networks, or professional communities.\nComfortable with cold outreach and building relationships from scratch.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/788f4c1f-5ee0-44ad-a3bd-2bdf98b6ea81","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/788f4c1f-5ee0-44ad-a3bd-2bdf98b6ea81/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"","additional":"<div>\n<div><strong>About Educative:</strong></div>\n<div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>\n</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Marketing and Sales","location":"Lahore","team":"Marketing","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1787817796466,"descriptionPlain":"","description":"<div>\n<p>Are you a curious, research-driven writer with a strong interest in technology and software development? Do you believe great content is about more than writing well and involves understanding users, identifying emerging trends, and delivering valuable information at the right time?</p>\n<p>Are you excited about using AI and generative content tools to research, create, edit, optimize, and scale high-quality technical content?</p>\n<p>If you answered “Yes,” then read on!</p>\n<p>As a Content Marketing Associate at Educative, you will help develop and manage content across Educative’s websites, microsites, community platforms, and external publishing channels. You will combine strong writing and editorial skills with AI-assisted content production, competitive intelligence, SEO, and audience research to build a proactive content engine that keeps Educative ahead of the market.</p>\n</div>","id":"aebecc5e-8559-47cb-a564-b59aa2da44c1","lists":[{"text":"In this role, you will be responsible for the following areas:","content":"<div>\n<p>In the role of Content Marketing Associate, you will:</p>\n\n<li>Research, edit, optimize, and publish technical blogs, newsletters, landing pages, guides, and other short- and long-form content.</li>\n<li>Use of GPT, Claude and other generative AI tools for content ideation, research, drafting, editing, optimization, repurposing, and scaling content production.</li>\n<li>Help develop and improve Educative’s content generation pipeline and workflows.</li>\n<li>Review and substantially improve content through research, fact-checking, editing, restructuring, and human judgment.</li>\n<li>Produce original content when strategic thinking, technical understanding, storytelling, or nuanced communication requires human-written content.</li>\n<li>Conduct ongoing competitor research across websites, microsites, Medium, DEV Community, Substack, newsletters, and other relevant platforms.</li>\n<li>Analyze competitor topics, formats, publishing strategies, messaging, SEO content approaches, and distribution channels to identify content gaps and opportunities.</li>\n<li>Take a proactive approach to market research by identifying emerging technology trends, developer interests, search behavior, and topics competitors may be investing in next.</li>\n<li>Translate market and competitive insights into actionable content ideas, editorial priorities, and new content initiatives.</li>\n<li>Develop user-focused landing page copy that clearly communicates value, addresses user needs, drives engagement, and supports conversion.</li>\n<li>Manage both on-page and off-page content initiatives across Educative’s websites, microsites, external platforms, and community channels.</li>\n<li>Manage content across multiple publishing accounts while maintaining consistent brand positioning and messaging.</li>\n<li>Adapt writing to different audience personas, platforms, content formats, and user intents while maintaining a consistent brand voice and tone.</li>\n<li>Apply SEO best practices, including keyword research, search intent analysis, content optimization, and internal linking, to improve organic visibility and user value.</li>\n<li>Monitor content performance and use data, audience insights, and market research to continuously improve content initiatives.</li>\n<li>Contribute to editorial calendars and manage content initiatives from ideation through execution and optimization.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with SEO, marketing, product, and subject-matter experts to create content aligned with both user needs and business objectives.</li>\n<li>Promote diversity, inclusivity, accessibility, and equity in the software engineering community through thoughtful and empathetic content.</li>\n\n</div>"},{"text":"About you:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>1-3 years of professional writing experience</li>\n<li>A writing-intensive academic background (e.g., B.A. in English or Journalism)</li>\n<li>Exceptional research, editing, and long-form writing skills, with strong writing samples.</li>\n<li>Exceptional long-form writing and research skills (and samples to prove it)</li>\n<li>Ability to communicate complex, technical ideas in accessible, digestible ways</li>\n<li>Ability to create content strategically and intentionally for specific audiences</li>\n<li>Working understanding of SEO best practices (experience using SEO tools is a plus)</li>\n<li>Meticulous eye for detail, comfortable editing the writing of others (and your own)</li>\n<li>Curious, growth-minded, eager to learn</li>\n<li>Self-starter, takes ownership of projects</li>\n<li>Passion for education, learning, teaching, mentoring</li>\n<li>Interested in the latest trends and developments in technology and software development</li>\n<li style=\"font-style: italic;\"><em>Computer programming experience (or familiarity with coding concepts) is a huge bonus</em></li>\n\n</div>"}],"text":"Content Marketing Associate","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<p>Are you a curious, research-driven writer with a strong interest in technology and software development? Do you believe great content is about more than writing well and involves understanding users, identifying emerging trends, and delivering valuable information at the right time?</p>\n<p>Are you excited about using AI and generative content tools to research, create, edit, optimize, and scale high-quality technical content?</p>\n<p>If you answered &ldquo;Yes,&rdquo; then read on!</p>\n<p>As a Content Marketing Associate at Educative, you will help develop and manage content across Educative&rsquo;s websites, microsites, community platforms, and external publishing channels. You will combine strong writing and editorial skills with AI-assisted content production, competitive intelligence, SEO, and audience research to build a proactive content engine that keeps Educative ahead of the market.</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/aebecc5e-8559-47cb-a564-b59aa2da44c1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/aebecc5e-8559-47cb-a564-b59aa2da44c1/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"This is a hybrid position (3 days a week in our Bellevue office).\n\n\n\nAbout Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">This is a hybrid position (3 days a week in our Bellevue office).</span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Operations","location":"Bellevue, WA","team":"Finance","allLocations":["Bellevue, WA"]},"createdAt":1752018710150,"descriptionPlain":"The Director of Finance and Operations is a strategic leader responsible for driving financial performance, operational efficiency, and scalable infrastructure across the organization. This role oversees finance, operations, legal, HR, and compliance in both the U.S. and Pakistan, enabling informed decision-making and sustainable growth. \n\n\nKey Objectives\n- Lead the company’s financial strategy, including budgeting, forecasting, reporting, and cash management.\n- Build and maintain a well-controlled, scalable, and efficient organization through strong financial and operational practices.\n- Ensure regulatory compliance in all operating jurisdictions (U.S. and Pakistan).\n- Partner with executive leadership to align financial and operational goals with business strategy.\n\n\nCore Responsibilities\n\nStrategic Leadership\n- Advise the CEO and senior leadership on strategic and operational issues using financial analysis and data-driven insights.\n- Support long-term planning and scenario modeling\n- Assess and manage risk and evaluate capital structure\n\nFinancial Forecasting & Cash Management\n- Lead short- and long-term financial forecasting, including revenue, expense, and margin projections.\n- Develop and manage robust cash flow models to ensure liquidity and support strategic decision-making.\n- Monitor working capital and optimize treasury operations, including disbursement cycles, receivables, and reserves.\n- Oversee cash management policies, daily bank reporting, and investment oversight.\n- Manage relationships with banking partners, external brokers, and financial service providers.\n- Oversee relationships with payment processors, ensuring accurate settlements, fee management, and compliance with financial reporting and reconciliation standards.\n\nFinancial Oversight\n- Oversee global financial reporting, close processes, and consolidations across multi-currency entities.\n- Review journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis to ensure accuracy and timeliness.\n- Ensure compliance with U.S. GAAP, international accounting standards, and local tax laws.\n- Lead all tax planning and compliance activities, including income, sales/use, payroll, franchise, and international tax filings.\n- Manage financial audits and reviews, and maintain strong relationships with external auditors.\n\nOperational Excellence\n- Lead company-wide financial management processes, including planning cycles, performance reporting, and scorecards.\n- Drive internal process optimization, cross-functional alignment, and systems integration.\n- Lead continuous improvement of ERP and financial tools (e.g., NetSuite).\n\nLegal, HR, and Administration\n- Oversee HR operations and partner with external consultants on compliance, performance, and compensation planning.\n- Manage legal activities including client and vendor contracts, partnership agreements, and regulatory compliance.\n- Support IT, facilities, and administrative operations to ensure operational continuity and scale.\n\n\nSupervisory Responsibilities\n- Accounting: Oversee U.S. and Pakistan accounting teams, budget preparation, and audits.\n- Finance & Analytics: Manage analytics, dashboards, and FP&A processes; develop team structure as the function scales.\n- HR: Guide HR consultants and internal teams on people operations and organizational design.\n\n\nSkills & Qualifications\n- Proven leadership in finance and operations roles, preferably in global or high-growth environments.\n- Strong knowledge of forecasting, budgeting, cash management, and GAAP accounting.\n- Proficient in NetSuite and financial analytics/reporting tools.\n- Excellent strategic thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills.\n- Strong organizational, compliance, and team management capabilities.\n\n","description":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">The </span><b>Director of Finance and Operations</b><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> is a strategic leader responsible for driving financial performance, operational efficiency, and scalable infrastructure across the organization. This role oversees finance, operations, legal, HR, and compliance in both the U.S. and Pakistan, enabling informed decision-making and sustainable growth. </span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Key Objectives</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead the company’s financial strategy, including budgeting, forecasting, reporting, and cash management.</div><div><b>- </b>Build and maintain a well-controlled, scalable, and efficient organization through strong financial and operational practices.</div><div><b>- </b>Ensure regulatory compliance in all operating jurisdictions (U.S. and Pakistan).</div><div><b>- </b>Partner with executive leadership to align financial and operational goals with business strategy.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Core Responsibilities</u></b></div><div><br></div><div><b>Strategic Leadership</b></div><div><b>- </b>Advise the CEO and senior leadership on strategic and operational issues using financial analysis and data-driven insights.</div><div><b>- </b>Support long-term planning and scenario modeling</div><div><b>- </b>Assess and manage risk and evaluate capital structure</div><div><br></div><div><b>Financial Forecasting &amp; Cash Management</b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead short- and long-term financial forecasting, including revenue, expense, and margin projections.</div><div><b>- </b>Develop and manage robust cash flow models to ensure liquidity and support strategic decision-making.</div><div><b>- </b>Monitor working capital and optimize treasury operations, including disbursement cycles, receivables, and reserves.</div><div><b>- </b>Oversee cash management policies, daily bank reporting, and investment oversight.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage relationships with banking partners, external brokers, and financial service providers.</div><div><b>- </b>Oversee relationships with payment processors, ensuring accurate settlements, fee management, and compliance with financial reporting and reconciliation standards.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Financial Oversight</b></div><div><b>- </b>Oversee global financial reporting, close processes, and consolidations across multi-currency entities.</div><div><b>- </b>Review journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis to ensure accuracy and timeliness.</div><div><b>- </b>Ensure compliance with U.S. GAAP, international accounting standards, and local tax laws.</div><div><b>- </b>Lead all tax planning and compliance activities, including income, sales/use, payroll, franchise, and international tax filings.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage financial audits and reviews, and maintain strong relationships with external auditors.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Operational Excellence</b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead company-wide financial management processes, including planning cycles, performance reporting, and scorecards.</div><div><b>- </b>Drive internal process optimization, cross-functional alignment, and systems integration.</div><div><b>- </b>Lead continuous improvement of ERP and financial tools (e.g., NetSuite).</div><div><br></div><div><b>Legal, HR, and Administration</b></div><div><b>- </b>Oversee HR operations and partner with external consultants on compliance, performance, and compensation planning.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage legal activities including client and vendor contracts, partnership agreements, and regulatory compliance.</div><div><b>- </b>Support IT, facilities, and administrative operations to ensure operational continuity and scale.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Supervisory Responsibilities</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Accounting: Oversee U.S. and Pakistan accounting teams, budget preparation, and audits.</div><div><b>- </b>Finance &amp; Analytics: Manage analytics, dashboards, and FP&amp;A processes; develop team structure as the function scales.</div><div><b>- </b>HR: Guide HR consultants and internal teams on people operations and organizational design.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Skills &amp; Qualifications</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Proven leadership in finance and operations roles, preferably in global or high-growth environments.</div><div><b>- </b>Strong knowledge of forecasting, budgeting, cash management, and GAAP accounting.</div><div><b>- </b>Proficient in NetSuite and financial analytics/reporting tools.</div><div><b>- </b>Excellent strategic thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills.</div><div><b>- </b>Strong organizational, compliance, and team management capabilities.</div><div><br></div>","id":"199a6e40-8e88-48c6-939a-8343d17a2800","lists":[],"salaryRange":{"min":165000,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-year-salary","max":220000},"text":"Director of Finance and Operations","country":"US","workplaceType":"hybrid","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">The </span><b>Director of Finance and Operations</b><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> is a strategic leader responsible for driving financial performance, operational efficiency, and scalable infrastructure across the organization. This role oversees finance, operations, legal, HR, and compliance in both the U.S. and Pakistan, enabling informed decision-making and sustainable growth. </span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Key Objectives</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead the company’s financial strategy, including budgeting, forecasting, reporting, and cash management.</div><div><b>- </b>Build and maintain a well-controlled, scalable, and efficient organization through strong financial and operational practices.</div><div><b>- </b>Ensure regulatory compliance in all operating jurisdictions (U.S. and Pakistan).</div><div><b>- </b>Partner with executive leadership to align financial and operational goals with business strategy.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Core Responsibilities</u></b></div><div><br></div><div><b>Strategic Leadership</b></div><div><b>- </b>Advise the CEO and senior leadership on strategic and operational issues using financial analysis and data-driven insights.</div><div><b>- </b>Support long-term planning and scenario modeling</div><div><b>- </b>Assess and manage risk and evaluate capital structure</div><div><br></div><div><b>Financial Forecasting &amp; Cash Management</b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead short- and long-term financial forecasting, including revenue, expense, and margin projections.</div><div><b>- </b>Develop and manage robust cash flow models to ensure liquidity and support strategic decision-making.</div><div><b>- </b>Monitor working capital and optimize treasury operations, including disbursement cycles, receivables, and reserves.</div><div><b>- </b>Oversee cash management policies, daily bank reporting, and investment oversight.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage relationships with banking partners, external brokers, and financial service providers.</div><div><b>- </b>Oversee relationships with payment processors, ensuring accurate settlements, fee management, and compliance with financial reporting and reconciliation standards.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Financial Oversight</b></div><div><b>- </b>Oversee global financial reporting, close processes, and consolidations across multi-currency entities.</div><div><b>- </b>Review journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis to ensure accuracy and timeliness.</div><div><b>- </b>Ensure compliance with U.S. GAAP, international accounting standards, and local tax laws.</div><div><b>- </b>Lead all tax planning and compliance activities, including income, sales/use, payroll, franchise, and international tax filings.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage financial audits and reviews, and maintain strong relationships with external auditors.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Operational Excellence</b></div><div><b>- </b>Lead company-wide financial management processes, including planning cycles, performance reporting, and scorecards.</div><div><b>- </b>Drive internal process optimization, cross-functional alignment, and systems integration.</div><div><b>- </b>Lead continuous improvement of ERP and financial tools (e.g., NetSuite).</div><div><br></div><div><b>Legal, HR, and Administration</b></div><div><b>- </b>Oversee HR operations and partner with external consultants on compliance, performance, and compensation planning.</div><div><b>- </b>Manage legal activities including client and vendor contracts, partnership agreements, and regulatory compliance.</div><div><b>- </b>Support IT, facilities, and administrative operations to ensure operational continuity and scale.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Supervisory Responsibilities</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Accounting: Oversee U.S. and Pakistan accounting teams, budget preparation, and audits.</div><div><b>- </b>Finance &amp; Analytics: Manage analytics, dashboards, and FP&amp;A processes; develop team structure as the function scales.</div><div><b>- </b>HR: Guide HR consultants and internal teams on people operations and organizational design.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b><u>Skills &amp; Qualifications</u></b></div><div><b>- </b>Proven leadership in finance and operations roles, preferably in global or high-growth environments.</div><div><b>- </b>Strong knowledge of forecasting, budgeting, cash management, and GAAP accounting.</div><div><b>- </b>Proficient in NetSuite and financial analytics/reporting tools.</div><div><b>- </b>Excellent strategic thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills.</div><div><b>- </b>Strong organizational, compliance, and team management capabilities.</div><div><br></div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"The Director of Finance and Operations is a strategic leader responsible for driving financial performance, operational efficiency, and scalable infrastructure across the organization. This role oversees finance, operations, legal, HR, and compliance in both the U.S. and Pakistan, enabling informed decision-making and sustainable growth. \n\n\nKey Objectives\n- Lead the company’s financial strategy, including budgeting, forecasting, reporting, and cash management.\n- Build and maintain a well-controlled, scalable, and efficient organization through strong financial and operational practices.\n- Ensure regulatory compliance in all operating jurisdictions (U.S. and Pakistan).\n- Partner with executive leadership to align financial and operational goals with business strategy.\n\n\nCore Responsibilities\n\nStrategic Leadership\n- Advise the CEO and senior leadership on strategic and operational issues using financial analysis and data-driven insights.\n- Support long-term planning and scenario modeling\n- Assess and manage risk and evaluate capital structure\n\nFinancial Forecasting & Cash Management\n- Lead short- and long-term financial forecasting, including revenue, expense, and margin projections.\n- Develop and manage robust cash flow models to ensure liquidity and support strategic decision-making.\n- Monitor working capital and optimize treasury operations, including disbursement cycles, receivables, and reserves.\n- Oversee cash management policies, daily bank reporting, and investment oversight.\n- Manage relationships with banking partners, external brokers, and financial service providers.\n- Oversee relationships with payment processors, ensuring accurate settlements, fee management, and compliance with financial reporting and reconciliation standards.\n\nFinancial Oversight\n- Oversee global financial reporting, close processes, and consolidations across multi-currency entities.\n- Review journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis to ensure accuracy and timeliness.\n- Ensure compliance with U.S. GAAP, international accounting standards, and local tax laws.\n- Lead all tax planning and compliance activities, including income, sales/use, payroll, franchise, and international tax filings.\n- Manage financial audits and reviews, and maintain strong relationships with external auditors.\n\nOperational Excellence\n- Lead company-wide financial management processes, including planning cycles, performance reporting, and scorecards.\n- Drive internal process optimization, cross-functional alignment, and systems integration.\n- Lead continuous improvement of ERP and financial tools (e.g., NetSuite).\n\nLegal, HR, and Administration\n- Oversee HR operations and partner with external consultants on compliance, performance, and compensation planning.\n- Manage legal activities including client and vendor contracts, partnership agreements, and regulatory compliance.\n- Support IT, facilities, and administrative operations to ensure operational continuity and scale.\n\n\nSupervisory Responsibilities\n- Accounting: Oversee U.S. and Pakistan accounting teams, budget preparation, and audits.\n- Finance & Analytics: Manage analytics, dashboards, and FP&A processes; develop team structure as the function scales.\n- HR: Guide HR consultants and internal teams on people operations and organizational design.\n\n\nSkills & Qualifications\n- Proven leadership in finance and operations roles, preferably in global or high-growth environments.\n- Strong knowledge of forecasting, budgeting, cash management, and GAAP accounting.\n- Proficient in NetSuite and financial analytics/reporting tools.\n- Excellent strategic thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills.\n- Strong organizational, compliance, and team management capabilities.\n\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/199a6e40-8e88-48c6-939a-8343d17a2800","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/199a6e40-8e88-48c6-939a-8343d17a2800/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Marketing and Sales","location":"Lahore","team":"Marketing","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1718970465711,"descriptionPlain":"Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.\nThis role reports to the Design Lead and will work closely with the marketing team to create a cohesive, memorable brand identity through digital design and online experiences. If you’re seeking a role where you can produce, design, contribute, and learn – this is it, and you will help define where we go!\n","description":"<div>\n<p>Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.</p>\n<p>This role reports to the Design Lead and will work closely with the marketing team to create a cohesive, memorable brand identity through digital design and online experiences. If you’re seeking a role where you can produce, design, contribute, and learn – this is it, and you will help define where we go!</p>\n</div>","id":"d9e7e06d-2877-4f41-9c7a-e4006c50a603","lists":[{"text":"Responsibilities for Designer","content":"\n<li>Translate business requirements and creative briefs into strong visual solutions.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with marketing and creative teams on strategic concepts and campaigns.</li>\n<li>Create compelling designs across web, social, paid ads, presentations, and other digital formats, including static and motion.</li>\n<li>Use AI-powered design and creative tools for ideation, exploration, prototyping, and production.</li>\n<li>Refine and art-direct AI-generated assets to meet Educative’s quality and brand standards.</li>\n<li>Help evolve and maintain a consistent visual identity across all brand touchpoints.</li>\n<li>Bring strong creative thinking, with a passion for strategy, ideas, typography, layout, and visual storytelling.</li>\n<li>Take ownership of projects, experiment with new creative technologies, and stay current with design and AI trends.</li>\n<li>Work comfortably in a fast-paced, collaborative startup environment.</li>\n"},{"text":"Qualifications for Designer","content":"\n<li>2–4 years of demonstrated experience in digital, graphic, or brand design.</li>\n<li>Proficient with Figma, Adobe tools, and modern AI-powered creative tools.</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of typography, layout, visual systems, and digital design.</li>\n<li>Ability to use AI as part of the creative process while maintaining strong human-led creative judgment.</li>\n<li>Ability to collaborate effectively, collect feedback, and rapidly iterate.</li>\n<li>Quality and deadline driven, with the ability to manage multiple projects efficiently.</li>\n<li>Prior experience working with startups and/or marketing teams.</li>\n<li>Experience developing and maintaining brand consistency across multiple channels.</li>\n<li>A strong portfolio showcasing creative thinking, layouts, typography, and digital design.</li>\n<li>Current on design, social media, AI, and visual culture trends.</li>\n<li>Experience with B2B or technology marketing is a plus.</li>\n"}],"text":"Graphic Designer","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<p>Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most &mdash; through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes &mdash; and how it shows up in the world.</p>\n<p>This role reports to the Design Lead and will work closely with the marketing team to create a cohesive, memorable brand identity through digital design and online experiences. If you&rsquo;re seeking a role where you can produce, design, contribute, and learn &ndash; this is it, and you will help define where we go!</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Educative has spent years helping developers build the skills that matter most — through hands-on, practical learning that actually sticks. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind brand, designed to change the way people think about learning in the age of AI. We're looking for the right people to help define what it becomes — and how it shows up in the world.\nThis role reports to the Design Lead and will work closely with the marketing team to create a cohesive, memorable brand identity through digital design and online experiences. If you’re seeking a role where you can produce, design, contribute, and learn – this is it, and you will help define where we go!\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/d9e7e06d-2877-4f41-9c7a-e4006c50a603","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/d9e7e06d-2877-4f41-9c7a-e4006c50a603/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Product","location":"Lahore","team":"Open positions","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1678264822845,"descriptionPlain":"Shape the experience millions of people will use to learn, and set the bar for what great looks like.\nWe have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. The design decisions you make here will be felt by millions of learners.\nThis is a rare opportunity to shape a category before its conventions are set. You'll make strong design calls without waiting for permission, treat ambiguity as your opening to define something great, and push design quality further than it's been before, with the freedom to explore bold ideas at every step.\nYou'll also join a design team that's rethinking what design means in the age of AI, building AI-ready design systems and workflows, not just AI-themed products. This isn't design-as-usual with an AI feature bolted on; it's a chance to help define the discipline itself.\n","description":"<div>\n<p><strong><em>Shape the experience millions of people will use to learn, and set the bar for what great looks like.</em></strong></p>\n<p>We have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. The design decisions you make here will be felt by millions of learners.</p>\n<p>This is a rare opportunity to shape a category before its conventions are set. You'll make strong design calls without waiting for permission, treat ambiguity as your opening to define something great, and push design quality further than it's been before, with the freedom to explore bold ideas at every step.</p>\n<p>You'll also join a design team that's rethinking what design means in the age of AI, building AI-ready design systems and workflows, not just AI-themed products. This isn't design-as-usual with an AI feature bolted on; it's a chance to help define the discipline itself.</p>\n</div>","id":"fc589071-9733-4173-be0a-ae432cc1593d","lists":[{"text":"In this role, you will be responsible for the following areas:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>Advocate relentlessly for the customer experience, obsessing over pain points until the product is more useful, enjoyable, and accessible.</li>\n<li>Partner closely with product managers on customer feedback and roadmap, then work with engineering to bring designs to life.</li>\n<li>Set design direction from user research and cross-team input, and take it from concept through wireframes to high-fidelity, tested prototypes.</li>\n<li>Present and defend your design decisions to cross-functional teams and senior leadership.</li>\n<li>Work within our design system, with the latitude to push it further as the product scales, and help define what “AI-ready” design means at Fenzo.</li>\n<li>Constantly raise the bar on design qualitym bring ideas nobody asked for but everybody needed.</li>\n\n</div>"},{"text":"About you:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>A track record of real design impact, whether that's a product you shaped solo, an experience you redesigned that moved real usage, or a system you scaled at a larger company. We care about what you drove, not how many years it took.</li>\n<li>Proven range across the full design process: research, wireframing, prototyping, visual design, interaction design, and usability testing.</li>\n<li>A portfolio with real depth in both interaction and visual design, not just polish.</li>\n<li>An eye for visual quality sharp enough to raise the bar for everyone around you.</li>\n<li>Comfort collaborating across product, engineering, and leadership, and defending your rationale to any of them.</li>\n<li>Genuine dissatisfaction with “good enough”, you're always pushing for better.</li>\n<li>A design degree (VCD, UX, Fine Arts, Interaction Design, or CS/HCI) or equivalent experience.</li>\n\n</div>"}],"text":"Product Designer","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<p><strong><em>Shape the experience millions of people will use to learn, and set the bar for what great looks like.</em></strong></p>\n<p>We have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. The design decisions you make here will be felt by millions of learners.</p>\n<p>This is a rare opportunity to shape a category before its conventions are set. You'll make strong design calls without waiting for permission, treat ambiguity as your opening to define something great, and push design quality further than it's been before, with the freedom to explore bold ideas at every step.</p>\n<p>You'll also join a design team that's rethinking what design means in the age of AI, building AI-ready design systems and workflows, not just AI-themed products. This isn't design-as-usual with an AI feature bolted on; it's a chance to help define the discipline itself.</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Shape the experience millions of people will use to learn, and set the bar for what great looks like.\nWe have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. The design decisions you make here will be felt by millions of learners.\nThis is a rare opportunity to shape a category before its conventions are set. You'll make strong design calls without waiting for permission, treat ambiguity as your opening to define something great, and push design quality further than it's been before, with the freedom to explore bold ideas at every step.\nYou'll also join a design team that's rethinking what design means in the age of AI, building AI-ready design systems and workflows, not just AI-themed products. This isn't design-as-usual with an AI feature bolted on; it's a chance to help define the discipline itself.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/fc589071-9733-4173-be0a-ae432cc1593d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/fc589071-9733-4173-be0a-ae432cc1593d/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Product","location":"Lahore","team":"Open positions","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1625870315611,"descriptionPlain":"Build the product that's redefining how the world learns, and own it like a founder.\nWe have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform, and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. We're looking for the person who helps decide what it becomes next.\nYou'll work directly with Educative's co-founders on a small, fast-moving team. This is an IC role, but not a quiet one: you'll own a real piece of the product, make calls backed by data, and see your decisions reach users within days, not quarters. If you build for impact and you're already three steps ahead of being told what to do, this is your room.\n \n","description":"<p><strong><em>Build the product that's redefining how the world learns, and own it like a founder.</em></strong></p>\n<p>We have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform, and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. We're looking for the person who helps decide what it becomes next.</p>\n<p>You'll work directly with Educative's co-founders on a small, fast-moving team. This is an IC role, but not a quiet one: you'll own a real piece of the product, make calls backed by data, and see your decisions reach users within days, not quarters. If you build for impact and you're already three steps ahead of being told what to do, this is your room.</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>","id":"659db28a-b4e5-4981-931f-16a8c35ff32c","lists":[{"text":"In this role, you will be responsible for the following areas:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>Identify, design, launch, and measure features that shape how learners discover and engage with Fenzo, with growth and experience as your north stars.</li>\n<li>Define the metrics that actually matter, track them rigorously, and tell leadership the truth about what's working and what isn't.</li>\n<li>Drive the roadmap for your product area, staying ahead of the competitive landscape and spotting the opportunity before someone else does.</li>\n<li>Partner tightly with engineering, design, and go-to-market to clear blockers and get real things shipped.</li>\n<li>Dig into root causes, build the business case, run the test, and make the prioritization call.</li>\n<li>Operate with real autonomy, set your agenda and move the org forward without waiting for one.</li>\n\n</div>"},{"text":"About you:","content":"\n<li>A track record of real impact, whether that's a feature you shipped solo, a project that moved a real metric, or a product you scaled at a larger company. We care about what you drove, not how many years it took.</li>\n<li>A hunger to own outcomes and move fast, you build the playbook rather than wait for one.</li>\n<li>Ability to cut through complexity, keeping ambitious projects on track, and making clear decisions when priorities compete.</li>\n<li>Experience owning the product vision, shaping go-to-market strategy, and leading design conversations. Ability to build design prototypes is required.</li>\n<li>Technical fluency, you don't need to write the code, but you can debate tradeoffs and timelines with engineers as an equal.</li>\n<li>A habit of using data to pressure-test assumptions and measure outcomes, not just report them.</li>\n<li>Clear, confident written and verbal communication.</li>\n<li>Bachelor's, Master's, or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.</li>\n<li>Experience with AI tools is required.</li>\n"}],"text":"Product Manager","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<p><strong><em>Build the product that's redefining how the world learns, and own it like a founder.</em></strong></p>\n<p>We have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform, and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. We're looking for the person who helps decide what it becomes next.</p>\n<p>You'll work directly with Educative's co-founders on a small, fast-moving team. This is an IC role, but not a quiet one: you'll own a real piece of the product, make calls backed by data, and see your decisions reach users within days, not quarters. If you build for impact and you're already three steps ahead of being told what to do, this is your room.</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Build the product that's redefining how the world learns, and own it like a founder.\nWe have spent a decade helping developers build the skills that matter most through hands-on, practical learning. Now we're building something entirely new. Fenzo is a first-of-its-kind AI learning platform, and the foundation for a growing portfolio of products built on top of it, from Courses and Books to Test Prep, and Flashcards, each generated and personalized in under a minute. We're looking for the person who helps decide what it becomes next.\nYou'll work directly with Educative's co-founders on a small, fast-moving team. This is an IC role, but not a quiet one: you'll own a real piece of the product, make calls backed by data, and see your decisions reach users within days, not quarters. If you build for impact and you're already three steps ahead of being told what to do, this is your room.\n \n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/659db28a-b4e5-4981-931f-16a8c35ff32c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/659db28a-b4e5-4981-931f-16a8c35ff32c/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Content","location":"Lahore","team":"TCE","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1625868712267,"descriptionPlain":"Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.\n\nYour responsibilities will include:\n\nCreate technical courses:\n• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.\n• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.  Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.\n• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.\n\nBuild expertise on Educative platform:\n• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.\n• May recommend product features and enhancements.  Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.\n\nDevelop people management skills:\n• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.\n","description":"<div>Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.</div><div><br></div><div>Your responsibilities will include:</div><div><br></div><div><b>Create technical courses:</b></div><div>• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.</div><div>• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.&nbsp; Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.</div><div>• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Build expertise on Educative platform:</b></div><div>• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.</div><div>• May recommend product features and enhancements.&nbsp; Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Develop people management skills:</b></div><div>• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.</div>","id":"c33cd8ef-043a-47b0-9454-561e6cd17e5c","lists":[{"text":"About you:","content":"<li>Strong hands-on engineer passionate about learning new programming languages and technologies, with excellent problem-solving skills.</li><li>Adept at communicating technically complicated topics simply and elegantly</li><li>Excellent written communication skills in English.</li><li>Self-directed, goal-oriented, and disciplined&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Strong time management and multitasking skills</li><li>Confident and comfortable presenting to different types of audiences, large and small</li><li>Hands-on experience with programming languages, such as C++, C#, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python, etc.</li>"}],"text":"Senior Technical Content Engineers","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.</div><div><br></div><div>Your responsibilities will include:</div><div><br></div><div><b>Create technical courses:</b></div><div>• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.</div><div>• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.&nbsp; Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.</div><div>• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Build expertise on Educative platform:</b></div><div>• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.</div><div>• May recommend product features and enhancements.&nbsp; Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Develop people management skills:</b></div><div>• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.\n\nYour responsibilities will include:\n\nCreate technical courses:\n• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.\n• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.  Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.\n• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.\n\nBuild expertise on Educative platform:\n• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.\n• May recommend product features and enhancements.  Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.\n\nDevelop people management skills:\n• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/c33cd8ef-043a-47b0-9454-561e6cd17e5c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/c33cd8ef-043a-47b0-9454-561e6cd17e5c/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Content","location":"Islamabad","team":"TCE","allLocations":["Islamabad"]},"createdAt":1664152856755,"descriptionPlain":"Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.\n\nYour responsibilities will include:\n\nCreate technical courses:\n• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.\n• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.  Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.\n• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.\n\nBuild expertise on Educative platform:\n• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.\n• May recommend product features and enhancements.  Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.\n\nDevelop people management skills:\n• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.\n","description":"<div>Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.</div><div><br></div><div>Your responsibilities will include:</div><div><br></div><div><b>Create technical courses:</b></div><div>• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.</div><div>• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.&nbsp; Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.</div><div>• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Build expertise on Educative platform:</b></div><div>• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.</div><div>• May recommend product features and enhancements.&nbsp; Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Develop people management skills:</b></div><div>• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.</div>","id":"0ee86a3d-2645-4c5e-8c72-6b8f6e68a1d5","lists":[{"text":"About you:","content":"<li>Strong hands-on engineer passionate about learning new programming languages and technologies, with excellent problem-solving skills.</li><li>Adept at communicating technically complicated topics simply and elegantly</li><li>Excellent written communication skills in English.</li><li>Self-directed, goal-oriented, and disciplined&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Strong time management and multitasking skills</li><li>Confident and comfortable presenting to different types of audiences, large and small</li><li>Hands-on experience with programming languages, such as C++, C#, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python, etc.</li>"}],"text":"Senior Technical Content Engineers (Islamabad)","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.</div><div><br></div><div>Your responsibilities will include:</div><div><br></div><div><b>Create technical courses:</b></div><div>• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.</div><div>• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.&nbsp; Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.</div><div>• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Build expertise on Educative platform:</b></div><div>• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.</div><div>• May recommend product features and enhancements.&nbsp; Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Develop people management skills:</b></div><div>• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Senior Technical Content Engineers (TCE) are distinguished by their ability to explain complex technical topics to learners. They create engaging technical content and work with subject matter experts to build courses for Educative learners.\n\nYour responsibilities will include:\n\nCreate technical courses:\n• Research, plan and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering audiences.\n• Review courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners.  Deliver feedback with clear and respectful language.\n• Monitor technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner needs.\n\nBuild expertise on Educative platform:\n• Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilize platform features in courses.\n• May recommend product features and enhancements.  Follow recommendation through prioritization, design and implementation.\n\nDevelop people management skills:\n• Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/0ee86a3d-2645-4c5e-8c72-6b8f6e68a1d5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/0ee86a3d-2645-4c5e-8c72-6b8f6e68a1d5/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Product","location":"Lahore","team":"Open positions","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1624301411455,"descriptionPlain":"Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.\n \nYou are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.\nIn this role, you will:\nWrite high quality, maintainable, reusable code following solid principles.\nIndependently clarify technical requirements, develop coding estimates and apply a broad range of design approaches to bring innovative solutions.\nReview code of other team members and provide constructive direction.\nConstantly strive to raise the bar on engineering excellence.\nDrive continuous improvement of software quality, customer experience and maintainability of products/features.\nMentor and lead developers by cultivating curiosity and deep technical understanding.\n \nNice to have:\nWe use the following technologies. Although these are not required for you to apply, you will need to be a fast learner and have a growth mindset.\nExperience with Google App Engine and Google Cloud.\nExperience in shipping production quality products using Python and Node.js.\nExperience in React/Redux/React Native.\nTypeScript, Next.js, and Tailwind CSS.\nExperience with Docker and Kubernetes.\nWorking experience with low-level systems and knowledge of Linux networking stack.\nExperience with AWS.\n \n","description":"<div>Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.</div>\n<div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>You are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.</div>\n<div><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></div>\n<div>Write high quality, maintainable, reusable code following solid principles.</div>\n<div>Independently clarify technical requirements, develop coding estimates and apply a broad range of design approaches to bring innovative solutions.</div>\n<div>Review code of other team members and provide constructive direction.</div>\n<div>Constantly strive to raise the bar on engineering excellence.</div>\n<div>Drive continuous improvement of software quality, customer experience and maintainability of products/features.</div>\n<div>Mentor and lead developers by cultivating curiosity and deep technical understanding.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>Nice to have:</strong></div>\n<div>We use the following technologies. Although these are not required for you to apply, you will need to be a fast learner and have a growth mindset.</div>\n<div>Experience with Google App Engine and Google Cloud.</div>\n<div>Experience in shipping production quality products using Python and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://Node.js\" class=\"postings-link\">Node.js</a>.</div>\n<div>Experience in React/Redux/React Native.</div>\n<div>TypeScript, <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://Next.js\" class=\"postings-link\">Next.js</a>, and Tailwind CSS.</div>\n<div>Experience with Docker and Kubernetes.</div>\n<div>Working experience with low-level systems and knowledge of Linux networking stack.</div>\n<div>Experience with AWS.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>","id":"09b4532f-3645-41bf-8546-e05b3448b8a0","lists":[{"text":"About you:","content":"\n<li>BS, MS or Ph.D. in computer science.</li>\n<li>Solid understanding of data structures and algorithms.</li>\n<li>Good knowledge of multithreading.</li>\n<li>Proficiency in at least one programming language, e.g., Python, JavaScript, Typescript, etc.</li>\n<li>Working knowledge of Git.</li>\n<li>Ability to work independently.</li>\n<li>Self-driven with a can-do attitude.</li>\n<li>Collaborative team player with excellent communication skills.</li>\n<li>Laser-focused on delivering high-quality features.</li>\n"}],"text":"Software Engineer (Entry-level)","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.</div>\n<div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>You are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.</div>\n<div><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></div>\n<div>Write high quality, maintainable, reusable code following solid principles.</div>\n<div>Independently clarify technical requirements, develop coding estimates and apply a broad range of design approaches to bring innovative solutions.</div>\n<div>Review code of other team members and provide constructive direction.</div>\n<div>Constantly strive to raise the bar on engineering excellence.</div>\n<div>Drive continuous improvement of software quality, customer experience and maintainability of products/features.</div>\n<div>Mentor and lead developers by cultivating curiosity and deep technical understanding.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>Nice to have:</strong></div>\n<div>We use the following technologies. Although these are not required for you to apply, you will need to be a fast learner and have a growth mindset.</div>\n<div>Experience with Google App Engine and Google Cloud.</div>\n<div>Experience in shipping production quality products using Python and <a class=\"postings-link\" href=\"http://Node.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Node.js</a>.</div>\n<div>Experience in React/Redux/React Native.</div>\n<div>TypeScript, <a class=\"postings-link\" href=\"http://Next.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Next.js</a>, and Tailwind CSS.</div>\n<div>Experience with Docker and Kubernetes.</div>\n<div>Working experience with low-level systems and knowledge of Linux networking stack.</div>\n<div>Experience with AWS.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.\n \nYou are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.\nIn this role, you will:\nWrite high quality, maintainable, reusable code following solid principles.\nIndependently clarify technical requirements, develop coding estimates and apply a broad range of design approaches to bring innovative solutions.\nReview code of other team members and provide constructive direction.\nConstantly strive to raise the bar on engineering excellence.\nDrive continuous improvement of software quality, customer experience and maintainability of products/features.\nMentor and lead developers by cultivating curiosity and deep technical understanding.\n \nNice to have:\nWe use the following technologies. Although these are not required for you to apply, you will need to be a fast learner and have a growth mindset.\nExperience with Google App Engine and Google Cloud.\nExperience in shipping production quality products using Python and Node.js.\nExperience in React/Redux/React Native.\nTypeScript, Next.js, and Tailwind CSS.\nExperience with Docker and Kubernetes.\nWorking experience with low-level systems and knowledge of Linux networking stack.\nExperience with AWS.\n \n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/09b4532f-3645-41bf-8546-e05b3448b8a0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/09b4532f-3645-41bf-8546-e05b3448b8a0/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Product","location":"Lahore","team":"Open positions","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1625615581993,"descriptionPlain":"Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.\n\nYou are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.\n","description":"<div>Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.</div><div><br></div><div>You are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.</div>","id":"5ddd53be-d3fa-4c87-9402-bcf2fbcf65df","lists":[{"text":"In This Role, You Will:","content":"<li>Write high quality, maintainable, reusable code following solid principles.</li><li>Independently clarify technical requirements, develop coding estimates and apply a broad range of design approaches to bring innovative solutions.</li><li>Review code of other team members and provide constructive direction.</li><li>Constantly strive to raise the bar on engineering excellence.</li><li>Drive continuous improvement of software quality, customer experience and maintainability of products/features.</li><li>Mentor and lead developers by cultivating curiosity and deep technical understanding.</li><li>Independently conduct quality review of 1-pagers and 6-pagers.</li><li>Evaluate root cause analysis (RCA) and facilitate RCA evaluation meetings.</li><li>Ensure the global platform architecture provides excellent agility, functionality, scalability, reliability, security, and performance.</li><li>Carry out a constant technology watch and stay aware of market opportunities and competitive threats.</li><li>Identify emerging technologies and set the direction of technological innovation and product investment.</li>"},{"text":"About You:","content":"<li>BS, MS or Ph.D. in computer science.</li><li>Solid understanding of data structures and algorithms.</li><li>Good knowledge of multithreading.</li><li>Proficiency in at least one programming language, e.g., Python, JavaScript, Typescript, etc.</li><li>Working knowledge of Git.</li><li>Ability to work independently.</li><li>Self-driven with a can-do attitude.</li><li>Collaborative team player with excellent communication skills.</li><li>Laser-focused on delivering high-quality features.</li>"},{"text":"Nice To Have:","content":"<li>Experience with Google App Engine and Google Cloud.</li><li>Experience in shipping production quality products using Python and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"postings-link\" href=\"http://Node.js\">Node.js</a>.</li><li>Experience in React/Redux/React Native.</li><li>TypeScript, <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"postings-link\" href=\"http://Next.js\">Next.js</a>, and Tailwind CSS.</li><li>Experience with Docker and Kubernetes.</li><li>Working experience with low-level systems and knowledge of Linux networking stack.</li><li>Experience with AWS.</li>"}],"text":"Software Engineer (Experienced)","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.</div><div><br></div><div>You are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Educative is connecting millions of developers around the world. We are a hyper growth platform for interactive text-based courses on many aspects of computer science, cloud computing, and advanced technologies.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses so they can get better at their job, find a better job or just experience the joy of learning.\n\nYou are an innovative and passionate developer focused on delivering a cutting-edge learning platform. You like to own deliverables end-to-end and have a meaningful influence on the final product. You are a builder. You like to work with fellow engineers and cross functional teams to share knowledge, imagine, design, develop, test, and launch features that wow our learners, authors and customers.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/5ddd53be-d3fa-4c87-9402-bcf2fbcf65df","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/5ddd53be-d3fa-4c87-9402-bcf2fbcf65df/apply"},{"additionalPlain":"About Educative:\nEducative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn. \n\nEducative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.\n\nOur learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.  With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.","additional":"<div><b>About Educative:</b></div><div>Educative is a hands-on learning platform for software developers of all levels. We were founded by industry veterans who understand first-hand the problems developers face staying on the cutting edge of modern technology. Educative's interactive, text-based courses are built to teach you the skills employers are looking for. We provide tools like in-browser coding environments and interview-focused assessments to help you practice as you learn.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Educative is connecting millions of developers worldwide to become a developer, grow their skills, or prepare for an interview.</div><div><br></div><div>Our learners rely on us to create engaging courses to get better at their job, find a better job, or experience the joy of learning.&nbsp; With the courses that you create, learners can maximize their success.</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Content","location":"Lahore","team":"TCE","allLocations":["Lahore"]},"createdAt":1624301842213,"description":"","descriptionPlain":"","id":"b065fdf1-680f-47e0-ad0f-08b67528ae98","lists":[{"text":"Your responsibilities will include:","content":"\n<li><strong>Create technical courses:</strong></li>\n<li>Research, plan, and create interactive text-based courses with hands-on programming assignments and projects for engineering <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://audiences.Review\" class=\"postings-link\">audiences.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://audiences.Review\" class=\"postings-link\">Review</a> courses created by others ensuring adherence to Educative standards for editorial and technical quality; and effective use of platform features to engage learners. Deliver feedback with clear and respectful <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://language.Monitor\" class=\"postings-link\">language.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://language.Monitor\" class=\"postings-link\">Monitor</a> technical developments to contribute to course strategy and ensure that Educative courses are responsive to learner <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://needs.Integrate\" class=\"postings-link\">needs.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://needs.Integrate\" class=\"postings-link\">Integrate</a> and leverage GenAI tools (e.g., Gemini, ChatGPT, Claude, GitHub Copilot) to strategically enhance and accelerate workflows in course research, content development, code generation, and quality <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://assurance.Apply\" class=\"postings-link\">assurance.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://assurance.Apply\" class=\"postings-link\">Apply</a> AI-assisted techniques to to deepen content accuracy, pedagogical effectiveness, and learner engagement, ensuring every course meets Educative’s high editorial and technical standards.</li>\n<li><strong>Build expertise on Educative platform:</strong></li>\n<li>Develop expertise on platform capabilities to effectively create courses and guide internal and external authors in fully utilizing platform features in <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://courses.May\" class=\"postings-link\">courses.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://courses.May\" class=\"postings-link\">May</a> recommend product features and enhancements. Follow the recommendation through prioritization, design, and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://implementation.Develop\" class=\"postings-link\">implementation.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://implementation.Develop\" class=\"postings-link\"><strong>Develop</strong></a><strong> people management skills:</strong></li>\n<li>Contribute to team development activities, such as campus and experienced hire recruiting, mentoring new team members, leading training sessions, etc.</li>\n"},{"text":"About you:","content":"\n<li>Strong hands-on engineer passionate about learning new programming languages and technologies, with excellent problem-solving <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://skills.AI\" class=\"postings-link\">skills.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://skills.AI\" class=\"postings-link\">AI</a> enthusiast with working knowledge of Generative AI concepts, Large Language Models (LLMs), and prompt engineering; hands-on experience using GenAI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, GitHub Copilot, or similar in a professional or technical <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://context.Adept\" class=\"postings-link\">context.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://context.Adept\" class=\"postings-link\">Adept</a> at communicating technically complicated topics simply and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://elegantly.Excellent\" class=\"postings-link\">elegantly.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://elegantly.Excellent\" class=\"postings-link\">Excellent</a> written communication skills in <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://English.Self-directed\" class=\"postings-link\">English.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://English.Self-directed\" class=\"postings-link\">Self-directed</a>, goal-oriented, and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://disciplined.Strong\" class=\"postings-link\">disciplined.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://disciplined.Strong\" class=\"postings-link\">Strong</a> time management and multitasking <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://skills.Confident\" class=\"postings-link\">skills.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://skills.Confident\" class=\"postings-link\">Confident</a> and comfortable presenting to different types of audiences, large and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://small.Hands-on\" class=\"postings-link\">small.</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://small.Hands-on\" class=\"postings-link\">Hands-on</a> experience with programming languages, such as C++, C#, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python, etc.</li>\n"}],"text":"Technical Content Engineer","country":"PK","workplaceType":"onsite","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"","descriptionBodyPlain":"","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/b065fdf1-680f-47e0-ad0f-08b67528ae98","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/educative/b065fdf1-680f-47e0-ad0f-08b67528ae98/apply"}]